Wake word models for the voice worker (src/channels/voice-mode-wakeword.ts)

These files are copied unmodified from livekit-wakeword
(https://github.com/livekit/livekit-wakeword, commit fb92cb3, version 0.2),
Copyright 2026 LiveKit, Inc., licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
(the LICENSE file in this directory):

- melspectrogram.onnx    src/livekit/wakeword/resources/melspectrogram.onnx
- embedding_model.onnx   src/livekit/wakeword/resources/embedding_model.onnx
- hey_livekit.onnx       examples/resources/hey_livekit.onnx

and, as test fixtures, src/channels/voice-mode-wakeword-fixtures/positive.wav and negative.wav
from its tests/fixtures/.

As livekit-wakeword documents them: melspectrogram.onnx is openWakeWord's
torchlibrosa mel-spectrogram front end, embedding_model.onnx is Google's
speech_embedding model (TF Hub google/speech_embedding/1), and hey_livekit.onnx
is LiveKit's conv-attention classifier for the phrase "hey livekit".

src/channels/voice-mode-wakeword.ts is a TypeScript port of livekit-wakeword's inference
pipeline (WakeWordModel.predict and WakeWordListener), not a copy of its code.

Google speech_embedding/1 is distributed under Apache-2.0 on TensorFlow Hub.
No openWakeWord pretrained classifier is included; hey_livekit is the LiveKit classifier.
